i inequality under \\(n\\) hyperplane symmetries ... Conjecture 4.1.1 (Logarithmic Brunn-Minkowski conjecture).\nChapter 4\n\nStability of log-Brunn-Minkowski and log-Minkowski inequality under \\(n\\) hyperplane symmetries\n\n## 4.1 Introduction\n\nIn this chapter, we establish stability versions of the log-Minkowski and log-Brunn-Minkowski conjectures under many hyperplane symmetries. First, recall that for \\(\\lambda \\in (0,1)\\), the \\(L_0\\) or logarithmic sum of two origin symmetric convex bodies \\(K\\) and \\(C\\) in \\(\\mathbb{R}^n\\) is defined by\n\n\\[\n(1-\\lambda)\\cdot K +_0 \\lambda \\cdot C = \\{x \\in \\mathbb{R}^n : \\langle x,u\\rangle \\le h_K(u)^{1-\\lambda} h_C(u)^\\lambda \\ \\forall u \\in S^{n-1}\\}.\n\\]\n\nIt is linearly invariant in the sense that \\(A((1-\\lambda)\\cdot K +_0 \\lambda \\cdot C) = (1-\\lambda)\\cdot AK +_0 \\lambda \\cdot AC\\) for \\(A \\in GL(n)\\). We recall here the long-standing and highly investigated equivalent conjectures - the log-Brunn-Minkowski and log-Minkowski conjecture for centered convex-bodies.\n\nConjecture 4.1.1 (Logarithmic Brunn-Minkowski conjecture). If \\(\\lambda \\in (0,1)\\) and \\(K\\) and \\(C\\) are convex bodies in \\(\\mathbb{R}^n\\) whose centroid is the origin, then\n\n\\[\nV((1-\\lambda)\\cdot K +_0 \\lambda \\cdot C) \\ge V(K)^{1-\\lambda}V(C)^\\lambda, \\qquad (4.1)\n\\]\n\nwith equality if and only if \\(K = K_1 + \\cdots + K_m\\) and \\(C = C_1 + \\cdots + C_m\\) compact convex sets \\(K_1,\\ldots,K_m,C_1,\\ldots,C_m\\) of dimension at least one where \\(\\sum_{i=1}^m \\dim K_i = n\\) and \\(K_i\\) and \\(C_i\\) are dilates, \\(i=1,\\ldots,m\\).\n\n75--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStability of the log-Brunn-Minkowski inequality in the case of many hyperplane symmetries (https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.02549)\nciteturn2academia13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.8 years ago; In the case of symmetries with respect to n independent linear 